<title>USA: U.S. DAP and ammonia steady, demand seen easing.</title>
<headline>U.S. DAP and ammonia steady, demand seen easing.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Prices for diammonium phosphate (DAP) and ammonia were steady compared with Friday, cash sources said.</p>
<p>But demand should ease soon as spring fertilizer applications were nearly finished in most of the Midwest and many farmers have turned to planting corn, dealers said.</p>
<p>			    Dlrs/short ton	 Chg from Friday</p>
<p>DAP central Fla		175-177	     unc</p>
<p>DAP central La Gulf	  188-189	     unc</p>
<p>Ammonia/La Gulf		170		   unc</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
